  "details": "Be present in VRChat, using the Oculus/Meta Quest 2 hardware either standalone or as a PC VR headset, it doesn't matter. \n\nBe active in a world, either with a couple of people or in a near-full lobby. \n\nSometimes as you move around, even a little, note that analogue stick input gets \"sustained\", almost emulating a severe case of 'stick drift'. \n\nUse the provided software tools in the Quest's operating system to check for drift and perform a calibration (even though no drift is present), then jump back into VRChat. \n\nNotice that the issue persists. \n\nTry new controllers. The issue persists.\n\nVerify that it is not a hardware defect by testing analogue input in other software titles (Rec Room for example). Notice that these issues do not persist across other software titles. \n\nReturn to VRChat to perform a sanity test, discover that the issue is exclusive to VRChat.",
